  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "North Bay Village consists of three islands—Harbor, North Bay, and Treasure—covering just 525 acres but steeped in South Florida history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://northbayvillage-fl.gov/about-us/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before 1940, most of what is now North Bay Village lay beneath Biscayne Bay, and dredging in 1940 created North Bay Island.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Bay_Village%2C_Florida"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The only dry land in the area was Broadcast Key, a five‑acre island where pioneer radio station WIOD began broadcasting in 1926.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Bay_Village%2C_Florida"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village was incorporated in 1945, shortly after Harbor and Treasure Islands were created by dredging and filling in the mid‑1940s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Bay_Village%2C_Florida"
    },
    {
